::SPEECH_U05_Pretest_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_Pretest_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.03
Question:
Unit 5 pretest item 1: Which choice shows readiness for revision, digital presentation, or publication skills?
{
=A. Use feedback to improve a speech draft#Correct. This choice supports publication-ready communication by improving clarity, collaboration, digital presentation, and audience understanding.
~B. Add more decoration instead of improving meaning#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully meet the communication purpose or collaboration standard.
~C. Ignore audience needs during final review#This choice reflects a misconception. Recheck revision, publication readiness, audience impact, or slide coherence.
~D. Let everyone edit without roles or version control#This choice weakens the communication product because it ignores how the audience will use or understand it.
}
::SPEECH_U05_Pretest_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_Pretest_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.04
Question:
Unit 5 pretest item 2: Which choice shows readiness for revision, digital presentation, or publication skills?
{
~A. Publish the first draft without reviewing it#This choice is incomplete because it does not support clear publication, revision, audience awareness, or digital presentation quality.
~B. Add more decoration instead of improving meaning#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully meet the communication purpose or collaboration standard.
=C. Revise language for clarity and standard English#Correct. This choice supports publication-ready communication by improving clarity, collaboration, digital presentation, and audience understanding.
~D. Let everyone edit without roles or version control#This choice weakens the communication product because it ignores how the audience will use or understand it.
}
